        "title": "Intro: Campus Se Company Tak Ka Financial Safar",
        "content": "Suno dost! Agar tum hostel room ke 10x10 square feet space mein baith kar apne laptop par Figma designs bana rahe ho, PyTorch model train kar rahe ho, ya doston ke saath milkar kisi college canteen problem ko solve karne ki app script kar rahe ho — toh congratulations! Tum sirf ek student nahi, balki ek **Student Founder** ho.\n\nIndian college ecosystem mein pichle 5-6 saalon mein ek massive socio-economic transformation aaya hai. Pehle 7th semester mein bas ek hi rigid target hota tha — IT service companies (TCS, Infosys, Wipro) ya core campus placements mein ek standard ₹4 Lakh to ₹8 Lakh per annum ka package uthana. Lekin aaj, Gen-Z campus founders hostel dorms se multi-crore startups build kar rahe hain. Steve Jobs ne Apple Garage se shuru kiya tha, Mark Zuckerberg ne Harvard dorm room se Facebook banaya tha, aur aaj India ke IITs, NITs, BITS, DTU, IIITs, aur Tier-2/Tier-3 colleges ke student founders India ki naye D2C, B2B SaaS, DeepTech, EdTech, aur FinTech revolution ko lead kar rahe hain.\n\nLekin... ek brutal financial reality check samajhna har college student founder ke liye sabse zaroori hai:\n> **\"Awesome pitch deck banana, college fest mein pitch competition jeetna, ya working prototype bana lena company chalana nahi hota. Global startup ecosystem mein 90%+ startups fail hone ka #1 reason bad idea nahi, balki FINANCIAL MISMANAGEMENT, BAD UNIT ECONOMICS, AUR CASH RUNNING OUT (RUNWAY KHATAM HONA) hota hai!\"**",
        "color": "#2563eb",
        "emoji": "🚀",
