        "title": "Business Entities Comparison for Student Founders (Part 3)",
        "content": "##### 4 Proven Zero-Balance Hacks for College Founders:\n\n1. **PSU Bank Basic Current Accounts (SBI / Punjab National Bank):**\n   - State Bank of India (SBI) offers basic business current accounts where MAB requirements are as low as **₹2,000** (Rural/Semi-urban) to **₹5,000** (Metro cities).\n2. **Neobanks & Digital First Corporate Banking (RazorpayX, Open, Jupiter Money):**\n   - Built specifically for modern tech startups in partnership with scheduled commercial banks (ICICI / Yes Bank). Offers zero-balance digital current accounts, automated vendor payouts, direct GST/TDS tax payments, and seamless API integration for your app!\n3. **DPIIT Startup India Bank Partnerships:**\n   - Leading banks (ICICI Bank Startup Ecosystem Account, HDFC SmartUp, Axis Startup Account) offer **1 to 2 Years Complete MAB Waiver** for DPIIT-recognized student startups!\n4. **College TBI Recommendation Letter:**\n   - If your startup is incubated at your college TBI (Technology Business Incubator), banks offer specialized Incubatee Corporate Accounts with waived balance rules.\n\n---\n\n#### Documents Required Checklist for Opening Current Account:\n\n| Document Category | Sole Proprietorship Firm | LLP (Limited Liability Partnership) | Private Limited Company (Pvt Ltd) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Identity & Address Proof of Founders** | Aadhar Card & PAN Card of Founder | Aadhar & PAN of all Partners | Aadhar & PAN of all Directors/Shareholders |\n| **Entity Proof Document 1** | Udyam MSME Registration Certificate | Certificate of Incorporation (COI) | Certificate of Incorporation (COI) issued by MCA |\n| **Entity Proof Document 2** | GST Registration / Shop & Establishment | Registered LLP Agreement | MOA (Memorandum) & AOA (Articles of Association) |\n| **Tax Registration Numbers** | Individual PAN + GSTIN (if applicable) | Entity PAN Card & TAN Card | Company PAN Card & TAN Card |\n| **Board Resolution / Authority** | Self-Declaration Letter | Partner Authorization Letter | Formal Board Resolution signed by Directors |\n| **Registered Office Address Proof** | Hostel Warden NOC / Rent Agreement + Electricity Bill | Rent Agreement + NOC from landlord + Utility Bill | Rent Agreement + NOC + Recent Electricity/Gas Bill |\n\n---\n\n### Udyam (MSME) Free Registration: The Ultimate Student Founder Cheat Code\n\nMinistry of Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSME), Government of India ek **100% Free digital portal** chalata hai jiska naam hai **Udyam Registration** (`udyamregistration.gov.in`).\n\n```\n                            ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                            │          THE UDYAM MSME BENEFIT ECOSYSTEM              │\n                            └────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────┘\n                                                           │\n         ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n         │                                               │                                               │\n   ┌─────▼─────┐                                   ┌─────▼─────┐                                   ┌─────▼─────┐\n   │  50% IP   │                                   │ COLLATERAL│                                   │  SECTION  │\n   │ DISCOUNT  │                                   │ FREE LOANS│                                   │  43B(h)   │\n   └─────┬─────┘                                   └─────┬─────┘                                   └─────┬─────┘\n         │                                               │                                               │\n   50% Off Govt Fees for                             CGTMSE Scheme up to                             Mandatory 45-Day\n   Patent & Trademark Filing                         ₹2 Cr Bank Credit                              Invoice Settlement Rule\n```\n\n#### 4 Game-Changing Benefits for Student Founders:\n\n1. **50% Flat Subsidy on IP, Patent & Trademark Filing Fees:**\n   - Standard government statutory fees for trademark registration (Form TM-A) for companies is ₹9,000 per class. Showing your Udyam Certificate instantly drops the fee by 50% down to **₹4,500**! Patent filing fees drop from ₹8,000 to ₹1,600!\n2. **Collateral-Free Bank Loans (CGTMSE Scheme):**\n   - Credit Guarantee Fund Trust for Micro and Small Enterprises (CGTMSE) scheme ke under registered micro units without any collateral security (bina zameen, ghar, ya gold girvi rakhe) ₹10 Lakh se ₹2 Crore tak ke bank credit limits apply kar sakti hain.\n3. **MSME Samadhaan & 45-Day Payment Rule (Section 43B(h) of Income Tax Act):**\n   - **The Ultimate Cash Flow Shield!** Big corporate clients or enterprise buyers often delay student vendor payments for 90 to 180 days, suffocating young startups.\n   - **Income Tax Section 43B(h) Enforcement:** If a corporate buyer does not pay a registered Micro/Small enterprise within **45 days** (if written agreement exists) or **15 days** (if no agreement exists), the buyer CANNOT claim that purchase as a deductible business expense in their Income Tax Returns for that year! The unpaid amount is added straight back to the buyer's taxable income, triggering heavy taxes. Result: Corporate accounts departments prioritize and clear student MSME bills on top priority!\n4. **Subsidized Electricity Tariffs & Govt Tender Exemption:**\n   - Exemption from Earnest Money Deposit (EMD) when bidding for government tenders and subsidies on testing lab charges.\n\n---",
