        "totalCardsInTopic": 3,
        "title": "Grants, Incubators & College Seed Funding (Part 3)",
        "content": "Ministry of Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSME) har saal **MSME Idea Hackathon** launch karta hai exclusively for college students and young innovators.\n- **Grant Support:** Up to **₹15 Lakh per approved idea** provided to host incubators for developing the prototype.\n- **Additional Support:** Up to **₹1.00 Crore** grant for procuring specialized plant & machinery for commercial production!\n\n---\n\n### College TBI (Technology Business Incubator) & AIC Ecosystem\n\nIndia mein 150+ NITI Aayog **Atal Incubation Centres (AICs)** aur DST-supported **STEP (Science and Technology Entrepreneurs Park)** incubators top engineering and management colleges (IITs, NITs, IIMs, BITS, DTU, IIITs, NIFT, Central Universities) mein operational hain.\n\n#### What Does a College Incubator Provide to Student Founders?\n1. **Physical Infrastructure:** Plug-and-play office desks, high-speed fiber internet, meeting rooms, and conference halls at ₹0 or nominal rent.\n2. **Specialized Lab Access:** Hardware, AI supercomputing clusters, bio-labs, 3D printing equipment.\n3. **Legal & Accounting Support:** In-house CA/CS panels to handle incorporation, GST, and ROC filings at subsidized student rates.\n4. **Direct Grant Facilitation:** Incubators act as official nodal implementation bodies for SISFS, NIDHI-PRAYAS, BIRAC, and TIDE 2.0 grants.\n5. **Investor Demo Days:** Direct access to Top Angel Networks (Indian Angel Network, Mumbai Angels, Venture Catalysts) and VCs (Peak XV, Accel, Blume).\n\n---\n\n### Master Comparison Table of Top Indian Student Grants\n\n| Grant / Scheme Name | Nodal Ministry / Govt Authority | Maximum Funding Amount | Funding Nature (Equity / Grant) | Ideal Target Domain | Key Eligibility Criteria | Application Window |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Startup India Seed Fund (SISFS)** | DPIIT / Ministry of Commerce | Up to **₹20 Lakh** (Grant) + **₹50 Lakh** (Debt) | Non-dilutive Grant / Soft Debt | Sector Agnostic (SaaS, D2C, B2B, AI) | DPIIT Recognized, < 2 years old | Open Year-round via portal |\n| **BIRAC BIG** | Dept of Biotech (DST) | Up to **₹50 Lakh** | Pure Non-Dilutive Grant | Biotech, Medtech, Bio-IT, AgriTech | Student/PhD or Startup < 5 years old | Twice a year (Jan & July calls) |\n| **NIDHI-PRAYAS** | Dept of Science & Tech (DST) | Up to **₹10 Lakh** | Pure Non-Dilutive Grant | Hardware, IoT, DeepTech, Robotics | Idea to Physical Prototype stage | Call-based via TBIs |\n| **NIDHI-EIR Fellowship**| Dept of Science & Tech (DST) | **₹10k - ₹30k / Month** (For 12 Months) | Monthly Living Stipend Grant | Sector Agnostic Innovators | Full-time student founder, no job | Call-based via TBIs |\n| **MeitY TIDE 2.0** | MeitY | **₹4 Lakh** (EiR) / **₹7 Lakh** (Grant) | Non-Dilutive Grant | Software, AI/ML, Electronics, IoT | Tech-driven business innovation | Call-based via TIDE Centers |\n| **MSME Idea Hackathon** | Ministry of MSME | Up to **₹15 Lakh** per idea | Non-dilutive Incubation Grant | Manufacturing, Cleantech, Agri | Open for all college students | Announced annually on portal |\n\n---",
