        "content": "```\nNet Realized Price (Post GST @ 18%):                     ₹422.88\n[-] Direct Product COGS (Herbal patch + Eco packaging):   ₹65.00\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\n= CM1 (Contribution Margin 1 / Product Margin):          ₹357.88 (84.6%)\n[-] Fulfillment (Courier ₹55 + Gateway ₹10 + RTO Buffer ₹25): ₹90.00\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\n= CM2 (Contribution Margin 2 / Order Margin):            ₹267.88 (63.3%)\n[-] Blended Meta Ad CAC per Order:                        ₹160.00\n-----------------------------------------------------------------\n= CM3 (Net Profit per First Delivered Order):             ₹107.88 (25.5% NET MARGIN!)\n```\n\n> **Outcome:** GlowBotanica reached **₹12 Lakh monthly revenue** fully bootstrapped and profitable, using profits to fund inventory without diluting equity to VCs!\n\n---\n\n### Case Study 3: Kunal's Hardware IoT Prototype & NIDHI-PRAYAS TBI Journey (AgriSense)\n\n#### Background:\nKunal (Mechanical Engg 4th Year) designed **AgriSense** — a solar-powered IoT soil moisture and nutrient sensor for precision agriculture.\n\n#### The Prototyping & Financial Strategy:\n- **Challenge:** Hardware manufacturing requires heavy upfront cash for custom PCB fabrication, sensors, injection molding, and testing machinery.\n- **Execution Step 1:** Incubated at College **Atal Incubation Centre (AIC)**. Secured free access to FabLab CNC machinery and oscilloscope testing tools (Saved ₹4 Lakh in capital equipment expenditure!).\n- **Execution Step 2:** Registered on **Udyam MSME Portal**. Applied for patent filing and claimed 50% statutory fee discount (Paid ₹4,500 instead of ₹9,000).\n- **Execution Step 3:** Won **₹10 Lakh DST NIDHI-PRAYAS Grant**. Manufactured 50 physical pilot units and deployed them across farms in Maharashtra.\n- **Execution Step 4 (MSME Samadhaan Protection):** When an agri-corporate client bought 30 units and delayed payment past 60 days, Kunal invoked **Section 43B(h) Income Tax Notice**. The corporate finance department cleared his ₹4.5 Lakh invoice within 48 hours!\n\n---\n\n### Case Study 4: Sneha's EdTech SISFS Grant & Pitch Deck Strategy (CodeVernacular)\n\n#### Background:\nSneha (MCA 2nd Year) created **CodeVernacular** — an AI-assisted coding platform teaching Data Structures & Algorithms in Indian regional languages (Hindi, Tamil, Telugu, Marathi).\n\n#### Grant Winning Strategy:\n- **Step 1:** Registered Private Limited entity and secured **DPIIT Startup India Recognition** within 4 days online.\n- **Step 2:** Applied for **MeitY TIDE 2.0 Grant** through her university incubator, securing **₹7 Lakh MVP Grant**.\n- **Step 3:** Applied for **Startup India Seed Fund Scheme (SISFS)** for ₹20 Lakh grant. Built a winning 5-slide financial model for the Incubator Seed Evaluation Committee:\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                   SNEHA'S WINNING 5-SLIDE FINANCIAL MODEL STRUCTURE                    │\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Slide 1: TAM-SAM-SOM Market Size (1.2 Crore Vernacular Engineering Students in India). │\n│ Slide 2: Unit Economics (CAC = ₹450, Course MRP = ₹3,499, Gross Margin = 82%).        │\n│ Slide 3: Milestone-Based Tranches (Tranche 1: Tech Infra, Tranche 2: Content Scale).   │\n│ Slide 4: 18-Month Cash Runway & Net Burn Projection Table.                             │\n│ Slide 5: Revenue & Profitability Trajectory (Targeting ₹50L ARR by Month 18).          │\n└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n- **Result:** SISFS committee approved **₹20 Lakh Equity-Free Grant** disbursed in 3 tranches based on platform user milestones!",
